Add motion levels, breadcrumb and a cheaper stage transition

The top bar gets four motion levels (Still, Quiet, Standard, Lively) and
a breadcrumb for the case, the current panel and the dossier trail.
Panels now draw themselves when they come into view, the money flow
wipes in from its sources, and Lively adds streaming ribbons, pulses and
count-ups.

The workspace becomes a small external store read through selectors,
which cuts the update callback of a stage zoom from about 40 ms to 9 ms.
GPU views hold still while a layout transition runs.

Headers and hints lose most of their explanatory text, "Fig." is gone
from panel numbers, and no text is italic.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Af3daEWcwnK2adxHHA5PiS


